    {
      "id": "claim_91ae4835b8e64652b68f503c4c27458e",
      "statement": "Zero-downtime migration: an authenticated /v1/admin/migrate?host=<new> call sets backupHost under a read-write mutex and then atomically flips isMigrating; while migrating, create/join-or-create requests are rejected via ForwardMigrate, which upgrades the connection and sends a going-away close (code 1001) whose reason is the backup host so clients reconnect to the new host.",
